{
  "id": "Compound::DB00860 - Disease::DOID:7148",
  "verbalization": "Prednisolone, a corticosteroid hormone receptor agonist, is linked to Rheumatoid Arthritis through its inclusion in the broader category of 17Alpha-Hydroxy Steroids, which includes Hydrocortisone. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways that demonstrate a causal or therapeutic link between Prednisolone and Rheumatoid Arthritis via Hydrocortisone. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone, through its inclusion in the corticosteroid hormone receptor agonist class, may exert a therapeutic effect on Rheumatoid Arthritis, as Hydrocortisone is known to treat this condition. The shared ancestry of Prednisolone and Hydrocortisone, through the 17Alpha-Hydroxy Steroid lineage, reinforces the potential for a mechanistic connection between these entities. The consistent presence of Hydrocortisone as a mediator in multiple pathways underscores the importance of corticosteroids in the treatment of Rheumatoid Arthritis, even though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
